    !/**
    !  @Version 1.0
    !  @Group Heaters
    !  @Summary Electric heater with overtemperature sensor or switch.
    !  Base component for an electric heater with analog overtemperature sensor or digital
    !  overtemperature switch.
    ! 
    ! 
    !  The BaseMotor object contains I/O signals for overtemperature supervision. You
    !  can choose between a digital temperature switch or an analog temperature sensor,
    !  but not both. The I/O signals are optional.
    ! 
    !  @b Object Graph
    !  @image orm_baseelheater_og.png
    ! 
    !  @h1 Configuration
    !  @b Component Configuration
    ! 
    !  - TempSwitch               Digital temperature switch
    !  - TempSensor               Analog temperature sensor
    !  - NoTempSwitchOrSensor     No temperature supervision
    ! 
    !  If TempSensor is selected, adjust the limits for HighHigh and High in the
    !  BaseTempSensor object (LimitHH and LimitH).
    ! 
    !  @b Signals
    !  Signals that has to be connected to I/O channels.
    ! 
    !  - TempSensor.Value     Ai (optional)
    !  - TempSwitch.Switch    Di (optional)
    !  
    !  @b Plc coding
    !  For plc coding the function object BaseElHeaterFo is used, if the heater
    !  contains a temperature switch or a temperature sensor. Otherwise there is
    !  no need for plc coding.
    !  @image orm_baseelheaterfo_fo.gif
    !  Create a function object in the plc editor and connect it to the current
    !  object with the connect function.
    ! 
    !  @b Simulate
    !  For simulation of the sensor value, use the plc object BaseElHeaterSim.
    !  
    !  @b See also
    !  @classlink BaseElHeaterFo basecomponent_baseelheaterfo.html
    !  @classlink BaseElHeaterSim basecomponent_baseelheatersim.html
    !  @classlink BaseTempSwitch basecomponent_basetempswitch.html
    !  @classlink BaseTempSensor basecomponent_basetempsensor.html 
    !*/
    Object BaseElHeater $ClassDef 169 09-OCT-2007 09:28:24.26
      Body SysBody 28-FEB-2023 14:19:10.80
